Only these route-local modules plus report-level claims explicitly marked canonical in `docs/state/theorem-state.yaml` are canonical Target C theorem sources at audit.50. Sections 110--121 are canonical report-level entries and are linked below. The exact train-coupled floor endpoint exclusion is also canonical; its detailed proof and independent audit are linked below. The file `95-protected-contact-creation-obstruction-audit.md` remains proof-only and is intentionally outside the canonical reading order.

## Scope rule

The §57 ZR/ZF theorem is on the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`, not the full source:

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3.
\]

Contact-isolated source points remain in the global configuration. Do not extend the affine-kernel conclusion to their coordinates.

## Current route

Audit.50 canonicalizes every valid post-104 result through normalized Section 123 and adds the full-core diameter-budget floor, the loaded-chord/train surplus floor, the formal \(\mu_D\to1\) equality-case companion below, and the promoted exact-floor endpoint exclusion. The strongest promoted explicit full-core carrier coefficient remains Section 118's

\[
0.9762439137425688\ldots .
\]

The full-core structural frontier is now two-level. On one carrier, Sections 120--121 give anisotropic return plus local Oler currency. Across the complete harmonic tiling, Sections 122--123 give

\[
\liminf {1\over D}\sum_r(L_r+P_{{\rm exc},r}-2d_r)
\ge {\pi\over2}(2-\sqrt3)
\]

and

\[
\sum_rP_{{\rm exc},r}\le10(e_{BB}-k).
\]

The clean source-level residual is the aggregate outer-walk detour `sum_r(L_r-2d_r)` coupled to `e_BB-k` and the actual loaded diameter graph. A closing theorem must upper-bound this same currency strongly enough to contradict Section 122 after the Section-123 payment, convert the forced detour into a source-preserving strict diameter decrease, or force an exact unit equilateral triangle.

The exact scalar floor endpoint is no longer live: canonical
`C-FULLCORE-FLOOR-ENDPOINT-EXCLUSION` excludes every full-core sequence with
`mu_D -> mu_TC` by unequal-shore pseudosegment extraction, phase-cut orientation
repair, phase-tail trimming, and the Section-76 source-hull diameter inequality.
Together with the canonical floor this yields an existential, non-explicit uniform
gap above `mu_TC`, but does not close the higher-surplus regime.

The promoted full-core budget floor is

\[
\mu_D:=\frac{e_{BB}+2s_C-3(d_H+s_Z)}D,
\qquad
\liminf_{D\to\infty}\mu_D\ge1.
\]

It removes only the subunit-\(\mu_D\) full-core regime. The promoted
`C-FULLCORE-TRAIN-SURPLUS-FLOOR` then uses the near-disk geometry to make every
loaded-loaded unit chord a hull side and couples the loaded-hull ledger to the
canonical train/interface currency, giving the stronger exact floor
\[
\liminf\mu_D\ge
\frac{2\pi+2\sqrt{\pi/(2\sqrt3)}}5
=1.6375621841815\ldots.
\]
It still supplies no upper bound on \(\mu_D\) and does not close the aggregate-detour
or macroscopic-container branches.

The canonical equality-case companion `C-FULLCORE-MU-ONE-CELL` adds:

\[
\mu_D\to1\Longrightarrow
\begin{cases}
\operatorname{diam}(P_*)=D-o(D),\\
\operatorname{area}(P_*)=\pi D^2/4-o(D^2),\\
\sum_{r\ne *}\operatorname{diam}(P_r)=o(D).
\end{cases}
\]

It also gives \(\operatorname{per}(P_*)=\pi D-o(D)\) and radius-\(1/2\) disk limits
after normalization. This does not force a unit triangle or supply a finite
source-preserving deformation.

The exact loaded-chord/train-floor audit is [`target_c_fullcore_train_coupled_surplus_floor_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md`](../../audits/target_c_fullcore_train_coupled_surplus_floor_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md), with proof report [`target_c_fullcore_train_coupled_surplus_floor_2026-09-14.md`](../../reports/target_c_fullcore_train_coupled_surplus_floor_2026-09-14.md).

The exact loaded-chord audit is [`target_c_fullcore_loaded_chord_elimination_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md`](../../audits/target_c_fullcore_loaded_chord_elimination_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md), with proof report [`target_c_fullcore_loaded_chord_elimination_2026-09-14.md`](../../reports/target_c_fullcore_loaded_chord_elimination_2026-09-14.md).

The equality-case concentration audit is [`target_c_mu_one_cell_concentration_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md`](../../audits/target_c_mu_one_cell_concentration_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md), with proof report [`target_c_mu_one_cell_concentration_2026-09-14.md`](../../reports/target_c_mu_one_cell_concentration_2026-09-14.md).

The exact train-coupled floor endpoint exclusion is audited in
[`target_c_fullcore_endpoint_unbalanced_pseudosegment_completion_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md`](../../audits/target_c_fullcore_endpoint_unbalanced_pseudosegment_completion_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md), with proof report
[`target_c_fullcore_endpoint_unbalanced_pseudosegment_completion_2026-09-14.md`](../../reports/target_c_fullcore_endpoint_unbalanced_pseudosegment_completion_2026-09-14.md). It excludes convergence to the endpoint and, together with the canonical floor, gives a non-explicit uniform gap above it.

The restricted finite oblique-lattice comparison is [`target_c_oblique_lattice_global_comparison_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md`](../../audits/target_c_oblique_lattice_global_comparison_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md), with proof report [`target_c_oblique_lattice_global_comparison_2026-09-14.md`](../../reports/target_c_oblique_lattice_global_comparison_2026-09-14.md). It is canonical only for one exact two-direction affine lattice under the displayed finite threshold; it leaves the inverse-diameter shear scale, non-affine grains, interfaces, holes, isolates, and macroscopic containers outside its scope.

The restricted affine-source comparison is canonical as C-OBLIQUE-LATTICE-COMPETITOR.
For a finite full-dimensional subset of one exact unit oblique lattice, the report
target_c_oblique_lattice_global_comparison_2026-09-14.md and its independent audit
target_c_oblique_lattice_global_comparison_independent_audit_2026-09-14.md give an
exact same-cardinality triangular-lattice source of strictly smaller diameter
above the displayed finite threshold. The surviving affine obstruction is only
the inverse-diameter angle excess O(D^{-1}); the theorem does not identify
arbitrary full-core minimizers with affine lattices.

The separate macroscopic-container branch remains open. Further decimal-only carrier optimization is secondary.

Binding corrections: Section 109's `r/(6C_T)` baseline is valid but not sharp; Section 111 gives the corrected `r/(3C_T)` joint-shore threshold. Section 121 is canonical only in its finite form: `G_loc=o(D^2)` does not imply `G_loc/d=o(1)`.

